        "original_id": "dddc4e48-15ad-56c4-a289-20d5ca5b05f1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: New York–New Jersey Line War\n- Places: disputed New York–New Jersey border, northeast coast of North America\n- Organizations: Province of New York, Province of New Jersey\n- Topics: British proprietary colonies, royal colonies\n\nFacts:\n- The Province of New York existed from 1664 to 1776 as a British proprietary colony and later as a royal colony on the northeast coast of North America.\n- The New York–New Jersey Line War, also called the N.J. Line War, was a series of skirmishes and raids that occurred from 1701 to 1765.\n- The New York–New Jersey Line War took place at the disputed border between the Province of New York and the Province of New Jersey.",
